* PIC16F818/819 Pin Definitions -- 18-pin PDIP/SOIC, 20-pin SSOP, and
* 28-pin QFN packages (all three share the identical 16-signal GPIO set;
* see the VDD/VSS/QFN note near the end of this header for what actually
* differs between them)
* Source: Microchip DS39598F "PIC16F818/819 Data Sheet", Table 1-2
*         (PIC16F818/819 Pinout Descriptions)
*
* Flagged for manual review (dual-function / non-obvious pins):
*   RA5/MCLR/VPP   -- default function is MCLR (active-low device Reset);
*                     RA5 GPIO requires the MCLRE Configuration bit cleared.
*                     Classified I (input-only) per the table's I/O/P Type
*                     column -- every sub-function (RA5, MCLR, VPP) is
*                     listed I or P, never O; RA5-as-GPIO cannot drive an
*                     output even with MCLRE cleared.
*   RA6/OSC2/CLKO, RA7/OSC1/CLKI -- primary oscillator pins; classified B
*                     per the table's own "Bidirectional I/O pin" text,
*                     but constrained/unavailable as GPIO once a
*                     crystal/resonator/external-clock oscillator mode is
*                     selected (CLKO becomes output-only in RC mode).
*   RB2/SDO/CCP1 and RB3/CCP1/PGM -- CCP1 alternate function appears on
*                     both pins in Table 1-2. Believed to be pin-remapped
*                     by a CCPMX-style Configuration bit (confirmed
*                     pattern on the sibling PIC16F87/88 family, which
*                     has the identical RB2/RB3 CCP1 dual-listing with an
*                     explicit CCPMX footnote) rather than simultaneously
*                     present on both pins. NOT independently confirmed
*                     against a PIC16F818/819-specific footnote in the
*                     source text available for this extraction --
*                     recommend verifying against the primary datasheet.
*                     Recorded as-is on each physical pin -- mux selection
*                     is a runtime/config concern outside this file's
*                     scope.
*   RB3/PGM        -- Low-Voltage ICSP Programming enable pin; additional
*                     dual-function on RB3 alongside the CCP1 item above.
*   RB6/PGC, RB7/PGD -- ICSP programming clock/data; shared with GPIO and
*                     with the Timer1 secondary oscillator (T1OSO/T1OSI).
*
* No directional-arrow Pin Diagram image was available for this
* extraction -- source material was text-only search-index snippets, not
* the rendered figure -- so the Step 5 arrow cross-check was not
* performed. Table 1-2 pin-type language (I/O/P columns) is the sole
* classification source.
*
* Table 1-2 and the Pin Diagram were reconstructed from search-engine-
* indexed text snippets across multiple independent third-party mirrors
* (primary microchip.com source disallows automated fetch); snippets were
* mutually consistent across mirrors but not verified against the
* original PDF directly. Recommend a final check against a primary copy
* before relying on this file, particularly the RB2/RB3 CCP1 item above.
*
* VDD and VSS occupy a single physical pin each (14 and 5 respectively)
* on the 18-pin PDIP/SOIC package -- no duplicates there. On the 20-pin
* SSOP, each occupies two physical pins (VDD: 15 & 16; VSS: 5 & 6) --
* same net each, still one V/G record. On the 28-pin QFN, each also
* occupies two physical pins (VDD and VSS both appear twice in the pin
* diagram), PLUS the datasheet recommends connecting the exposed thermal
* pad to VSS as well -- still just one V/G record; the pad isn't a
* numbered signal pin and isn't given its own record.
*
* The 28-pin QFN additionally has several NC (No Connect) pins, used only
* to keep the 16-signal GPIO set physically routable on that pinout --
* not recorded here, since NC isn't a signal in this file's format.

D PIC16F818/819 18/20-Pin Enhanced Flash Microcontrollers with nanoWatt Technology
P PIC16F818 PIC16F819 PIC16LF818 PIC16LF819

V VDD
B RA0 AN0
B RA1 AN1
B RA2 AN2/VREF-
B RA3 AN3/VREF+
B RA4 AN4/T0CKI
I RA5 MCLR/VPP
B RA6 OSC2/CLKO
X
K SIMCLK

B RA7 OSC1/CLKI
B RB0 INT
B RB1 SDI/SDA
B RB2 SDO/CCP1
B RB3 CCP1/PGM
B RB4 SCK/SCL
B RB5 SS
B RB6 T1OSO/T1CKI/PGC
B RB7 T1OSI/PGD
G VSS

*
* End of pin definitions file
*